---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import TldrBox from '../../components/TldrBox.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { site } from '../../content';
const path = '/for/digital-products';
const title = 'Shopify SMS apps for digital products: access and permission';
const desc = 'Compare conditional SMS and lifecycle fits for digital downloads, licenses and courses, with entitlement checks, recovery ownership and contribution measurement.';
const faqs = [
  { question: 'Does a digital purchase authorize promotional SMS?', answer: 'Treat fulfillment and marketing permission separately. A paid order can justify delivering the purchased service through an appropriate service channel; it does not establish promotional SMS permission for the payer, gift recipient or learner. Check the intended person, channel, purpose and current permission before each marketing send.' },
  { question: 'Which system should decide whether access is active?', answer: 'Use the designated license, download or course system as the entitlement authority, reconciled with payment and refund records. A marketing profile or message click must not activate, reissue or revoke access. Assign support an authenticated recovery path when those systems disagree.' },
  { question: 'Can Postscript or Klaviyo fit a digital product store?', answer: 'Postscript is a candidate for a team operating an SMS audience and campaign program. Klaviyo is a candidate when a team needs customer data and marketing automation across channels. Evaluate the required digital product events, identity mapping, cancellation behavior and current account costs in a pilot; neither choice establishes entitlement authority by itself.' },
  { question: 'Should a purchase stop every automation?', answer: 'Retire the matching checkout reminder and stale launch offer when payment is confirmed. Keep separately eligible fulfillment, access recovery and requested onboarding jobs under their own rules. A refund, access change or marketing withdrawal requires a fresh decision for each affected purpose rather than a universal automation rule.' },
];
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
  <section class="relative overflow-hidden py-16 md:py-24">
    <div class="container">
      <a class="link text-sm" href="/for">All store types</a>
      <p class="badge mt-6">Digital downloads, licenses and courses</p>
      <h1 class="hero-title mt-5 max-w-5xl">Choose SMS around permission and access truth</h1>
      <p class="mt-7 max-w-3xl text-xl leading-9">A payer, a gift recipient and a course account holder may be three different people. Choose a marketing tool only after deciding who owns access, who may receive each message, and what ends a queued reminder.</p>
      <p class="mt-5 max-w-3xl text-lg leading-8">A download link, activation email or course invitation serves a purchase. An upgrade offer serves marketing. Keep those purposes separate, even when one customer needs both. The operating fixtures below are hypothetical proposals, not merchant results or executed tests.</p>
      <div class="mt-9 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/apps">App directory</a>
        <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/guides/email-sms-coordination">Channel coordination</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="container pb-12">
    <TldrBox title="Two conditional evaluation paths" picks={[
      { label: 'SMS program ownership', tool: 'Postscript', reason: 'Consider for SMS audience building and campaign messaging when an operator can maintain permission, send rules and digital entitlement exclusions.' },
      { label: 'Customer data and automation', tool: 'Klaviyo', reason: 'Consider for marketing automation using customer data across channels when the team can map and reconcile license, download or course events.' },
    ]} />
    <article class="prose-shopify card mb-8">
      <h2>Compare the work each supplier would own</h2>
      <p><a class="link" href="https://postscript.io/">Postscript</a> currently describes SMS list building and message delivery, alongside additional channels. A proposed fit is a permissioned launch or upgrade SMS program for a store whose access service is already reliable. Give the campaign owner a verified eligible audience and a current destination; keep license issuance with the fulfillment owner. Check event availability, exportable permission history and cancellation acknowledgments in the actual account before relying on this design.</p>
      <p><a class="link" href="https://www.klaviyo.com/solutions/marketing-automation">Klaviyo</a> currently describes marketing channels, customer data and integrations. A proposed fit is coordinated education and relevant follow-up when a team can join commerce and learning or license states without merging unrelated people. Confirm the specific connector or custom event fields, update latency, identity resolution and send-time filtering. An integration listing alone does not prove that a course completion or revoked license is available.</p>
      <p>These are distinct starting points for evaluation, not a mandatory combination or a ranking. Ask each shortlisted supplier for current country/channel availability, subscription and usage charges, billable profiles, message segments, carrier fees, event limits, support and migration costs at your expected peak. The price and implementation effort depend on your account. Keep an existing tool if it can meet the same operating requirements at an acceptable total cost.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="prose-shopify card mb-8">
      <h2>Write the authority and identity contract first</h2>
      <p>Store an order ID and line item, product/version, payer customer ID, intended recipient, verified account ID, license or enrollment ID, purpose, event version and timestamps. Record who can approve a gift claim, seat assignment or entitlement change. An email address or shared phone number is a contact point, not proof that two records belong to the same person. Resolve ambiguous claims through authenticated support; do not reveal license keys or private course progress in a marketing text.</p>
      <p>The commerce payment record owns paid, pending, failed and refunded amounts. The designated fulfillment/license/course service owns issued, unclaimed, active, expired, suspended and revoked access. Reconcile both before declaring a person eligible. Paid does not prove successful delivery; a link click does not prove a completed download or activated license; course enrollment does not prove a lesson was started or completed. If a source lacks a state, label it unknown instead of inferring it from engagement.</p>
      <p>Assign an authorized operator to approve manual fulfillment, gift reassignment and recovery. An approval-pending job must not promise access. Approval should retire the pending-approval reminder and allow only the next authorized service step; rejected or cancelled approval retires its reminder without granting access. A refund decision and a revocation decision need explicit policy and separate confirmations; do not assume either system changed because the other did.</p>
      <p><a class="link" href="https://help.shopify.com/en/manual/products/digital-service-product/digital-downloads">Shopify's Digital Products documentation</a> describes file/link delivery and download-link deactivation. Verify the actual app and delivery method installed in your store. Hosted courses and software license servers can have different authority and revocation behavior. Removing a marketing link cannot recall a downloaded file or prove that external course access ended.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="prose-shopify card mb-8">
      <h2>Separate the message queues</h2>
      <div class="overflow-x-auto">
        <table class="data-table">
          <thead><tr><th>Purpose</th><th>Entry and destination</th><th>Exit and owner</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>Checkout reminder</td><td>Known checkout and current channel permission; return to that checkout</td><td>Payment, cancellation, withdrawal or expiry retires this reminder; campaign owner</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Paid access delivery</td><td>Confirmed paid line and authorized fulfillment; authenticated access page</td><td>Successful delivery/claim, refund hold or entitlement denial closes or redirects job; fulfillment owner</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Activation recovery</td><td>Issued but unactivated entitlement, verified account and unresolved issue; secure recovery page</td><td>Activation, reissue supersession, revocation, expiry or support resolution; support owner</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Requested course onboarding</td><td>Active enrollment and the applicable service/request basis; correct lesson/account</td><td>Completion, withdrawal from onboarding, suspension or expired enrollment; course owner</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Upgrade or next-course offer</td><td>Relevant eligible customer with current promotional permission; compatible product/version</td><td>Purchase of that offer, withdrawal, conflict with entitlement/refund state or offer expiry; marketing owner</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p>A purchase stops the matching abandonment and obsolete acquisition offers. It can begin authorized fulfillment and separately requested onboarding. An open access incident pauses related upgrade pressure while support resolves it; it need not cancel unrelated, independently eligible service jobs. Marketing withdrawal retires affected promotional queues promptly and must not be reversed by a late payment webhook or restored profile. Define purpose-specific opt-outs rather than treating SMS withdrawal as cancellation of a purchased course.</p>
      <p>For each channel retain the permission source, disclosure, timestamp, purpose, recipient and withdrawal history. Gift purchasers cannot donate promotional permission for recipients. Recheck eligibility, recipient-local sending policy, current entitlement and destination immediately before dispatch. Route uncertain identity, timezone or permission cases to review. Verify current applicable requirements with the responsible adviser; this page does not certify legal compliance. See <a class="link" href="/guides/consent">permission operations</a>.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="prose-shopify card mb-8">
      <h2>Proposed workload fixtures for a pilot</h2>
      <p>Use these fictional workloads to specify expected behavior before enabling sends. They are not evidence of improvements, completed pilots or successful integrations.</p>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>Paid ebook, unclaimed link:</strong> reconcile the paid line with issuance; send the authorized delivery to the verified recipient, not an upgrade offer disguised as recovery.</li>
        <li><strong>Gifted course:</strong> keep payer receipts with the payer, invite the intended learner through a claim process, and seek that learner's own marketing permission.</li>
        <li><strong>Pending manual approval:</strong> queue no activation promise; approval closes the pending reminder, while rejection records a terminal reason and routes the service response to its owner.</li>
        <li><strong>License activation:</strong> stop the unused-license reminder on confirmed activation; preserve compatible requested setup guidance under its own rules.</li>
        <li><strong>Reissued license:</strong> authenticate recovery, invalidate the superseded credential where supported, and cancel old activation reminders before the new version becomes eligible.</li>
        <li><strong>Partial bundle refund:</strong> map the refunded line to its entitlement; retain valid sibling access and stop only the affected upsell/recovery jobs.</li>
        <li><strong>Revoked course access:</strong> retire lesson nudges and access offers for that enrollment; confirm external revocation independently and give support a documented appeal path.</li>
        <li><strong>Course completed:</strong> close the unfinished-lesson queue; a relevant next-course offer needs separate promotional eligibility and an active offer.</li>
        <li><strong>Download limit reached:</strong> route to authenticated support; do not automatically reset access from a marketing click or infer theft from repeated attempts.</li>
        <li><strong>New version release:</strong> distinguish included updates from paid upgrades by license terms; avoid charging an owner for an included entitlement.</li>
        <li><strong>Live cohort deadline:</strong> use the actual enrollment close and remaining capacity; retire the offer at closure and do not invent physical stock scarcity for unlimited files.</li>
        <li><strong>Late refund after queued SMS:</strong> reconcile authoritative current state at dispatch, cancel the job and record why; escalate if the provider already accepted a send that cannot be recalled.</li>
        <li><strong>Shared household phone:</strong> hold an ambiguous course-progress text and verify the person; do not merge learners or disclose their learning states.</li>
        <li><strong>Duplicate payment event after withdrawal:</strong> deduplicate the fulfillment action, retain withdrawal and prevent the old promotion from re-entering.</li>
      </ol>
    </article>
    <article class="prose-shopify card mb-8">
      <h2>Retire jobs and recover without replaying old offers</h2>
      <p>Key a job by order line, entitlement, recipient, purpose and version. Deduplicate provider event IDs and record event time separately from receipt time. Retry transient delivery failures with bounded attempts and an expiry; reuse the same operation key. Reconcile newer authoritative state before accepting a delayed event. A late paid event cannot overwrite a later refund or revocation. Unknown event ordering should hold the job for reconciliation.</p>
      <p>On approval, purchase, activation, reissue, completion, withdrawal or expiry, close the affected queue with a terminal reason and cancellation acknowledgment. Recheck already scheduled provider jobs; marking a profile suppressed is not proof of cancellation. Keep a minimal audit trail so retries cannot resurrect retired work. A fresh eligible purpose needs a new decision and version, not a reset of an old campaign.</p>
      <p>Assign support an authenticated access-recovery handoff containing order line, entitlement state, last confirmed event and failed operation, without exposing secrets. Never place reusable license keys or unrestricted download tokens in promotional URLs. Track unresolved cases until a named owner confirms recovery or denial. Keep payer communications separate from recipient access support where identity differs.</p>
      <p>Before migration, export permission and withdrawal evidence, terminal jobs, active entitlement mappings and unresolved tickets. Pause overlapping sends, reconcile records and pilot one purpose with a named owner. Stop on wrong-person delivery, stale access promises or lost withdrawals. Roll back by disabling the new trigger, cancelling its scheduled work and restoring the prior verified routing; preserve terminal states and dedupe history. Do not bulk replay the backlog. Resume only after the affected accounts and queues have been reconciled.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="prose-shopify card mb-8">
      <h2>Measure orders, licenses and people separately</h2>
      <p>Define a fixed observation window and randomize eligible customers into comparable treatment and holdout groups, keeping all of a customer's licenses and orders in one group. Preserve promised fulfillment and necessary support for both groups. Count distinct paid orders for purchase conversion, distinct issued licenses for activation rate, and distinct enrolled learners for course completion. State whether refunds reduce the order count or appear separately; do not change that rule mid-pilot. A payer's three licenses are one customer, not three acquired customers.</p>
      <p>Illustrative arithmetic only: 200 eligible customers in treatment generate $4,000 in sales after discounts and refunds. Subtract $500 in royalties/payment costs, $300 in allocated platform and message costs and $200 in incremental support: contribution is $3,000, or $15 per eligible customer. If 100 comparable holdout customers produce $1,300 contribution under the same cost rules, that is $13 each, a proposed comparison of $2 per eligible customer. This is not measured lift. Do not subtract discounts or refunds again after using net sales.</p>
      <p>Separately, 60 activations from 80 issued licenses would be 75%; 24 completions from 40 enrolled learners would be 60%. Neither denominator is messages sent. Report access incidents per fulfilled order, failed deliveries per attempt, opt-outs per delivered promotional recipient and recovery time per resolved ticket, with unresolved tickets visible. Decide the reporting unit before rollout and avoid counting duplicate events as additional orders, activations or customers.</p>
      <p>Compare expected peak costs and support workload, not platform-attributed revenue alone. Proceed only after the pilot verifies identity mapping, access destinations, permission checks, purpose-specific exits, cancellation, deduplication and rollback in the installed configuration. Read the <a class="link" href="/guides/pricing">cost worksheet</a> and <a class="link" href="/guides/campaign-restraint">campaign planning guide</a> with those boundaries in mind.</p>
    </article>
  </section>
  <FaqSection faqs={faqs} />
</BaseLayout>
